Trail Mate licensing
====================

Copyright (c) 2026 Liu Weikai (Vic Liu), for original contributions in which
the maintainer holds copyright. Third-party copyrights are retained.

Original material
-----------------

Original code, documentation and other copyrightable material in which the
maintainer holds the necessary rights is offered under LICENSES/MIT.txt.
This grant excludes upstream-derived material, contributions owned by others
without their permission, and material whose rights have not been established.
In mixed files, each portion retains its applicable copyright and license.

Reticulum and LXMF
------------------

Trail Mate includes implementations derived from Mark Qvist's reference works:

* https://github.com/markqvist/Reticulum
  Copyright (c) 2016-2026 Mark Qvist, unless otherwise noted.
* https://github.com/markqvist/LXMF
  Copyright (c) 2020-2026 Mark Qvist, unless otherwise noted.

All RNS/LXMF-derived portions, including code generated from those sources and
subsequently regenerated derivatives, retain the original copyright and the
Reticulum License. No MIT, GPL or AGPL alternative is granted for those portions.

The complete derivative notice is in LICENSES/Reticulum-Derivatives.txt.
Original upstream notices are retained in LICENSES/Reticulum-RNS.txt and
LICENSES/Reticulum-LXMF.txt. Preserve all applicable copyright and permission
notices when copying or distributing the covered material.

Correction of earlier statements
-------------------------------

Earlier blanket AGPL descriptions and any claim of maintainer copyright over
Mark Qvist's RNS/LXMF-derived material were mistakes and are void for those
portions. This correction applies to earlier revisions and releases containing
that material, not only to the current source tree. The original copyright and
Reticulum License grants remain applicable regardless of the earlier labels.

Valid prior grants for material a licensor had authority to license are not
revoked. The previous root AGPL text is retained in LICENSES/AGPL-3.0.txt.

Other components and distribution
---------------------------------

Third-party components retain their original licenses and notices. TMAP's
eligible maintainer-owned originals have the additional MIT grant recorded in
LICENSES/TMAP-MIT.txt and docs/licensing/TMAP_RELICENSING.md; third-party rights
and the fixed historical package's metadata are preserved.

LXST requires separate authorization for the Trail Mate derivative. Including
its upstream license text does not supply that permission.

There is no blanket license grant for every combined firmware or package.
Affected releases remain paused pending LXST authorization and resolution of
combined-license compatibility. Read LICENSING.md, NOTICE.md,
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and docs/licensing/reticulum-sources.csv for scope.
